Fixed. The bug was at `src/import_merge.ts:7` where the comparison `b.url === inc.url` was case-sensitive.

**Change:** Added a `normalizeUrl` helper that lowercases URLs (via `new URL(...).href` when valid, falling back to plain lowercasing for malformed strings) and used it in the `find` comparison. Hostnames differing only in case (`example.com` vs `EXAMPLE.com`) now match, so the incoming bookmark is merged into the existing entry (unioning tags) instead of being added as a duplicate.

**Verified:** A test case with existing `https://example.com/a` and incoming `https://EXAMPLE.com/a` produces a single entry with unioned tags `["x","y"]`, keeping the existing entry's id.


